        terms: ['tabulated data', 'numerical integration', 'equally spaced ordinates', 'mean values', 'measured waveform'],
        definition:
          'When a waveform is known only from measurements at equally spaced instants rather than as a formula, the Euler integrals are replaced by numerical averages. Taking N equally spaced ordinates over one period, the constant term is twice the mean of the values, each cosine coefficient is twice the mean of the values multiplied by the corresponding cosine, and each sine coefficient likewise. The method is exactly the trapezoidal rule applied to the Euler integrals, and its accuracy is limited by the number of samples: with N points, harmonics above N over two cannot be resolved at all.',
        takeaway: 'Replace each integral by twice the mean of the sampled products, and expect to resolve harmonics only up to N over two.',
