        complexity: { best: 'one substitution or one multiplication per rule', avg: 'the correction terms in the advance rule are the only fiddly part', worst: 'multiple shifts and damping combined need careful bookkeeping', note: 'The delay rule is exactly why the Z-transform suits difference equations, which are built from delayed terms.' },
