        definition:
          'Solution methods expect the problem in a particular shape, so any formulation must first be converted. Canonical form has a maximisation objective with all constraints as less-than-or-equal inequalities and all variables non-negative. Standard form, used by the simplex method, requires all constraints as equalities with non-negative right-hand sides. Converting between them uses a small set of moves: minimising a function is maximising its negative, a greater-than-or-equal constraint reverses on multiplication by minus one, and a variable unrestricted in sign is replaced by the difference of two non-negative ones.',
