        definition:
          'Each iteration moves to an adjacent vertex by bringing one variable into the basis and removing another. The entering variable is chosen from the objective row as the one whose increase improves the objective fastest, conventionally the most negative entry. The leaving variable is determined by the ratio test: divide each right-hand side by the corresponding positive entry in the entering column and choose the smallest non-negative ratio, which identifies the constraint that becomes binding first. The intersection of the entering column and the leaving row is the pivot element.',
